[
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43309\">#43309</a>, I am turning one of the fields of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Convexity.StdSimplex#doc\">docs#Convexity.StdSimplex</a> into an <code>extends</code> clause:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Diff\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"gd\">-structure StdSimplex (R : Type u) [LE R] [AddCommMonoid R] [One R] (X : Type v) where</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+structure StdSimplex (R : Type u) [LE R] [AddCommMonoid R] [One R] (X : Type v) extends</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>  /-- The weights of the `StdSimplex` as a `Finsupp`. -/\n<span class=\"gd\">-  weights : X →₀ R</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+  weights : X →₀ R where</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>  /-- All weights are non-negative. -/\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>  nonneg : 0 ≤ weights\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 622660901,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1788901693
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unfortunately, this is a syntax error, because <code>extends</code> clauses do not accept docstrings. Should this be fixed, for consistency with fields?</p>",
        "id": 622660937,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1788901714
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can do this instead:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StdSimplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">One</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- All weights are non-negative. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The weights of the `StdSimplex` as a `Finsupp`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"n\">add_decl_doc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StdSimplex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">weights</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 622661534,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788901969
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes that is indeed what I have done in the PR.</p>",
        "id": 622661692,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1788902030
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah I see</p>",
        "id": 622662359,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788902201
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, I feel like the wanted change</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StdSimplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">One</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The weights of the `StdSimplex` as a `Finsupp`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- All weights are non-negative. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is not necessarily easy to read; because the <code>weights</code> subobject field is so similar to the other field that at first you're confused about why there is a <code>where</code> in that spot. But I guess I can accept this with slighly different formatting:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StdSimplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">One</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The weights of the `StdSimplex` as a `Finsupp`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- All weights are non-negative. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>... but maybe the <code>add_decl_doc</code> version is still nicer to look at? At least, it feels more \"compact\"</p>",
        "id": 622664177,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788902956
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I agree that putting <code>weights</code> and <code>nonneg</code> at the same indentation level is confusing (that's exactly why I requested the change on the PR!)</p>",
        "id": 622664928,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1788903180
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My reasoning (which I already explained in-person) is that an <code>extends</code> clause is a glorified field</p>",
        "id": 622665608,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1788903406
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, to highlight the fact that it is a field, maybe</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StdSimplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">One</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The weights of the `StdSimplex` as a `Finsupp`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- All weights are non-negative. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weights</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>would maybe be nice but I'm not sure it's a good idea to introduce an entirely new syntax for extending structures.</p>",
        "id": 622665872,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788903484
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this version would start to look weird if there are multiple things we're extending by. But I agree it would be nice if we could have docstrings on the <code>extends</code></p>",
        "id": 622668552,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1788904231
    }
]